    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the prince de ligne sounds closer, but there's something even more specific i remember. i have this feeling of being someone very close to the power in france, maybe an advisor or someone who could influence the king's decisions without being the main face of it. i remember a specific scent—old parchment and heavy candle wax—and the feeling of being in a room where the fate of Europe was being decided in whispers. do you think there's anyone from the french court around that time who fits that profile? someone who worked in the shadows of the great statesmen?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
